# HakiOS fragment: the Qualcomm SM8450 family (Snapdragon 8 Gen 1: "waipio", "taro") -- what is true of the SoC, whatever device it is in.
# The processor has eight cores (1x Cortex-X2, 3x Cortex-A710, 4x Cortex-A510) and the biggest is core 7.
# socinfo: the chip reports itself as SM8450 (msm-id 457 in the phone's own tree) through SMEM at 0x80900000, the same as the
# reference phone, so the driver's built-in default fits.
CONFIG_SOC="sm8450"
CONFIG_CPUS=8
CONFIG_BOOTCPU=7
CONFIG_SOCINFO=y
CONFIG_HAKIOS_SOCINFO=y
# Not here yet, and why:
#   CPUFREQ  the driver's EPSS is the SC7280's 0x18591000; this SoC's is 0x17d91000 (the phone's tree, qcom,cpufreq-hw),
#            a code change and not an argument.
#   THERMAL  the sensor table is the phone's own: tools/dt-thermal.py on this device's tree. The two TSENS blocks are at
#            0xc263000 and 0xc265000, the same as the driver's defaults.
#   PMIC     the PMIC arbiter's addresses are this SoC's; not read yet.
